# Line endings, settled in one place.
#
# The repository stores LF (that is what is in the index and in every commit).
# Without this file a Windows checkout writes CRLF into the working tree, git
# then reports every file in the repository as modified, and a real one-line
# change becomes impossible to find in `git status`. This pins the checkout to
# match what is stored.
#
# After adding this, one-time cleanup for a working tree that already drifted:
#     git add --renormalize .
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gz  binary
*.db  binary
